{"id": "20526437", "revid": "21678789", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20526437", "title": "Proamanullin", "text": "Promanullin is a cyclic nonribosomal peptide. It is an amatoxin, all of which are found in the mushroom genus \"Amanita\".\nToxicology.\nLike other amatoxins, proamanullin is an inhibitor of RNA polymerase II. Promanullin has a specific attraction to the enzyme RNA polymerase II. Upon ingestion, it binds to the RNA polymerase II enzyme, effectively causing cytolysis of hepatocytes (liver cells)."}
