{"id": "20527097", "revid": "277086", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20527097", "title": "Francis Ferran", "text": "Francis Patrick Ferran (died 10 June 1923) was an Irish Sinn F\u00e9in politician and medical practitioner. He was elected unopposed as a Sinn F\u00e9in Teachta D\u00e1la (TD) to the 2nd D\u00e1il at the 1921 elections for the Sligo\u2013Mayo East constituency. He opposed the Anglo-Irish Treaty and voted against it. He was elected as an anti-Treaty Sinn F\u00e9in TD at the 1922 general election but did not take his seat. He died while imprisoned by the pro-Treaty government during the Irish Civil War at the Curragh Camp in 1923."}
