{"id": "20527645", "revid": "27015025", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20527645", "title": "Electoral district of Monmouth", "text": "The Electoral district of Monmouth was a single-member electoral district of the Tasmanian House of Assembly. It was based in the rural hinterland to the north of the state capital, Hobart.\nThe seat was created in a redistribution ahead of the 1903 state election out of the former seats of Brighton and Richmond, and was abolished when the Tasmanian parliament adopted the Hare-Clark electoral model in 1909. It had a single member during its existence, Thomas Hodgman."}
