{"id": "20528541", "revid": "1318951994", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20528541", "title": "Dirk Baberowski", "text": "Dirk Baberowski is a German player. He is one of the most successful players of the game. He has won three , tying him in second place with Jon Finkel. Two of those victories were won at team Pro Tours with his teammates of \"Phoenix Foundation\", Kai Budde and Marco Blume.\nIn 2008, Barberowski was voted in the . He was inducted during the in Memphis.\nCareer.\nDirk Baberowski qualified for (PT) Chicago due to a 12th place at Grand Prix Zurich on 31 May 1998. PT Chicago on 25\u201327 September 1998 featured \"--\" Rochester Draft. Despite being his first PT appearance Baberowksi managed to win the tournament, drafting a green-white deck, widely considered a horrible color combination in that format.\nOther than a 2nd-place finish behind teammate Kai Budde at Grand Prix Amsterdam, most of the remaining season consisted of mediocre finishes at professional events. Baberowski managed another 2nd place at the European Championships in Berlin at the end of the season, though. A 63rd place at the in Tokyo sufficed to take home the award.\nThe only notable finish in the next two PT seasons was a top 8 finish, again at a Pro Tour in Chicago. After that Dirk banded up with Kai Budde and Marco Blume to form the team \"Phoenix Foundation\". Together they swept back to back team Pro Tours in New York (2001) and Boston (2002), also winning the Osaka team Master in between. The following season Phoenix Foundation managed another final day appearance in Boston (2003). Phoenix Foundation disbanded thereafter with the members quitting professional Magic.\nAccomplishments.\nOther accomplishments:"}
{"id": "20528542", "revid": "27199084", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20528542", "title": "Llucmajor (Barcelona Metro)", "text": "Llucmajor is a Barcelona Metro station, on L4.\nPart of the extension of that line from Guinard\u00f3 into Nou Barris opened in , it takes its name from \"Pla\u00e7a de Llucmajor\", the previous name of Pla\u00e7a de la Rep\u00fablica, the central square of the district. The station is located under Passeig de Verdum, between carrer de Lorena and carrer de Formentor, and can be accessed from that intersection and from Jardins d'Alf\u00e0bia."}
