{"id": "20531571", "revid": "196446", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20531571", "title": "Francisco Marins", "text": "Francisco Marins, (November 23, 1922 - April 10, 2016) was a Brazilian writer. He was the author of a series of books for children, about the Taquara-P\u00f3ca farm. Marins also writes historic novels set in the colonial Brazilian hinterland. He was born in Prat\u00e2nia, Estado de S\u00e3o Paulo, which was at the time part of Botucatu.\nMarins has sold more than 5,000,000 books, which have been translated into fifteen languages, and is the only Brazilian writer in the European collection \"Delphin\", that features classics of children's literature around the world.\nFrancisco Marins is a member of the \"Academia Paulista de Letras\"."}
